{"name":"Notre Dame","hex":"#c6c5bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Notre Dame","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Notre-Dame de Paris.","Ellipsis of University of Notre Dame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Notre_Dame"}],"entries":[{"title":"Notre-Dame de Paris","blocks":[{"text":"Notre-Dame de Paris, often referred to simply as Notre-Dame, is a medieval Catholic cathedral and basilica on the Île de la Cité, in the 4th arrondissement of Paris, France. It is the cathedral church of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Notre-Dame_de_Paris%2C_4_October_2017.jpg/330px-Notre-Dame_de_Paris%2C_4_October_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame_de_Paris","wikidata":"Q2981"},{"title":"University of Notre Dame","blocks":[{"text":"The University of Notre Dame du Lac is a private Catholic research university in Notre Dame, Indiana, United States. The university was founded in 1842 by members of the Congregation of Holy Cross, a Catholic religious order of priests and brothers. Its main campus covers 1,261 acres in a suburban setting and has landmarks such as the Golden Dome main building, Sacred Heart Basilica, the Grotto of Our Lady of Lourdes, the Word of Life mosaic mural, and Notre Dame Stadium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/University_of_Notre_Dame_seal_%282%29.svg/330px-University_of_Notre_Dame_seal_%282%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Notre_Dame","wikidata":"Q178848"},{"title":"Dame","blocks":[{"text":"Dame is a traditionally British honorific title given to women who have been admitted to certain orders of chivalry. It is the female equivalent of Sir, the title used by knights. Baronetesses in their own right also use